        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: സൂര്യോദയം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സൂര്യോദയം — sūryōdayaṁ — \"sunrise\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സൂര്യോദയം കാണാൻ ഞങ്ങൾ പുലർച്ചെ എഴുന്നേറ്റു. sūryōdayaṁ kāṇān ñaṅṅaḷ pularcce eḻunnēṟṟu. We got up at dawn to watch the sunrise."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സൂര്യൻ, the sun, plus ഉദയം, rising: the vowels join as -ോ-."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സൂര്യോദയം (sūryōdayaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit sūryodaya, sunrise, from sūrya, \"the sun\", and udaya, \"rising\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
